<title>USA: U.S. Aug natgas stocks rise 9 pct. pts to 60 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug natgas stocks rise 9 pct. pts to 60 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. natgas storage levels in August rose nine percentage points to 60 percent of capacity, as the traditional start of the heating season neared and cash prices fell below the $2 per million British thermal units mark.</p>
<p>The Reuter survey of 24 firms with working gas capacity of 2.11 trillion cubic feet (tcf) showed stocks of 1270.1 billion cubic feet were still five points below 1995.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
